{"id": "EUVD-2026-91481", "enisaUuid": "a923d23a-fb8a-30f4-94f9-1718ace33834", "description": "YesWiki before 4.6.7 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows page editors to make the server fetch arbitrary URLs via the url parameter of the Bazar valeur action. Attackers can embed the action with a champ parameter in wiki markup to reach loopback or internal services and partially read responses rendered into the page.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T11:38:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-04T14:59:42", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/YesWiki/yeswiki/security/advisories/GHSA-6rvf-7pwm-6j44", "https://github.com/YesWiki/yeswiki/commit/22a5260b0381824e01d340ce9457c4adb9e18b23", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/yeswiki-before-4.6.7-ssrf-via-bazar-valeur-action-url-parameter"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-104470", "GHSA-32r4-8mw9-77h4"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "37126da2-15b2-3842-b6c1-a591c1995ec5", "product": {"name": "yeswiki", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.6.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9b916876-0181-3bdb-9a82-b0d6569ae2e7", "vendor": {"name": "YesWiki"}}], "isExploited": false}